{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/414505-lunar-appearance-what-do-you-want-it-to-do","id":414505,"title":"Lunar Appearance - What do you want it to do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-21T15:40:51-08:00","id":414505,"title":"Lunar Appearance - What do you want it to do?","content":"So, I really get the feeling that Shape-shifting Knacks are getting folded back into the Lunar charm-set, since Knacks as a category really only existed to prevent Eclipse Castes from getting them.<br /> <br /> Now assuming that that's the case, Appearance can rely directly on shape-shifting instead of illusions and hypnotism (although it still could). Things like Changing Plumage Mastery, Twin-Faced Hero etc. will probably be becoming part of the charmset again, yet charms like [Become-whomever-the-target-most-wishes-to-see] (I can't recall the name, I'll edit as soon as I find it), which rely on &quot;illusion&quot;, which I personally really enjoy and think fitting for the splat, might not make it in (or at least change to fit the &quot;physicality&quot; theme). Because of this, and because I'm kind of creatively narrow, I'm having trouble thinking of new things that could <i>work</i> within that thematic that aren't already published.<br /> <br /> So, what do you want Appearance Charms to do and/or how would you make their effects manifest? As a sub-topic, this question can apply to social/mental attributes as a whole - how would you apply &quot;physicality&quot; to Intelligence, or Manipulation? Would you shift it towards other themes associated with the Moon? Would you revamp existing effects in any particular way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:39:37-08:00","id":414601,"title":"","content":"Intimidation charms is the only thing that comes off my head, making yourself look ferociously scary with Appearance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:48:33-08:00","id":414610,"title":"","content":"It depends on what Appearance itself does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T17:27:01-08:00","id":414629,"title":"","content":"The Twin horrors of &quot;what if Eclipse get these charms&quot; and &quot;Silver-Solar&quot; magic were bad -- but I respected Knacks in the sense that they seemed like variant &quot;Permanent&quot; charms for an early splat. Mind you, <b>Alchemicals and Infernals</b> did it better - but it was a start (and if they become charms, I hope they're permanent ones).<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> I wouldn't shift &quot;physicality&quot; toward Mental and Social attributes - that'd just reinforce Lunars as nimrods (in both senses of the word). <br /> <br /> Existing charms that rock:<br /> Perception (Holistic Knowledge Transmission, Nest Names the Wasp, Outland-Navigating Guile, Eyes as Moonbeams Method), Intelligence (Flesh-Sculpting Art, Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick, Argent Weaver Art, Burgeoning Wyld Infliction, Phantom Crossfire Feint), Wits (Thousandfold Wasp Dance, Cold Breath of the Moon) and the Charisma charms (for Solar Mates) come to mind. <br /> <br /> As for Appearance, itself. Hm. You could probably fold a lot of stuff into it - look at Alchemicals. Gender-change, camouflage, hide obvious signs of being Exalted (or emulate other Exalts, like Alchemicals &amp; Sidereals can do), and probably a few Fate-related stuff (Alchemicals get it so they can masquerade with the Loom; how about Lunars getting something so they can masquerade better among other denizens, if I decide to roam through the Underworld or Malfeas?). <br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> <b>I think a core thing to address</b> is that Appearance is a <b>social, not physical</b> Attribute. It should be more <b>active</b>, not passive.<br /> <br /> Less &quot;I have Appearance 5, everyone should worship me&quot; and more like &quot;I have Manipulation 5 - but <i>I still need to come up with plots to manipulate people into them</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Appearance could be used for <i>Camouflage</i> -- Alchemicals can look human &amp; literally write themselves into the Loom of Fate with Appearance charms, to blend in; Infernals can acquire fake fates and reshape themselves with various charms; Lunars should use some of the wyld-magic (or whatever) to better emulate others and blend into their territory. What if a Lunar wants to roam Autochotonia, masquerading as a machine-god? What if a Lunar wants to stalk the underworld pretending to be another dead thing? We had some good Knacks --- and could eventually acquire Spirit Charms -- but I feel like they were kept out of reach due to fear of game-breaking combos (like multiple actions and such), thus denying more aesthetic/superficial things (like if a Lunar wanted to learn the baby-crafting Neomah charm in order to pretend to be one). At the least, we need a natural way to &quot;reskin&quot; mutations (without animal features) so we can use those to emulate others powers (obviously faking them, but still, it'd help).<br /> <br /> Existing charms that do this are Hide of the Cunning Hunter (hide tattoos, scars, blemishes), One of the Herd (don't stand out of the crowd).<br /> <br /> Hm.<br /> <br /> A simple Awe charm to ensure people <i>notice</i> and pay attention to them (if they're within line-of-sight) as a precursor to using other charms (ie, the Solar might give better speeches - but the Lunar is <i>noticeable</i>, even <i>distracting</i> when they appear on the same street). I don't mean Perfect Symmetry (improve your MDV), or New Friend Aroma (create an Intimacy in the target) --- and fuck all those charms that remind us that our magic is &quot;almost as good as the Lawgivers&quot; (but more expensive) --- but things where Appearance trumps Skill. Your Solar might be <i>glib</i>, but the Lunar <i>demands attention by merely walking in</i>. Your Solar might be <i>a great hostess</i>, but the Lunar <i>leaves men thinking Venus just visited the room</i>. <br /> <br /> Solars have <i>personality</i>.<br /> Lunars have <i>looks</i>.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022103109001164\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sciencedirect.com/science...22103109001164</a><br /> <br /> A fear inducing charm - built on being inhumanly hideous or beautiful. Really, there aren't a lot of fear-effects (IMO). Glowing lights and magic might be spooky, <i>but a shapeshifting 9-foot monster</i> should be the most terrifying. Charms that terrify you <b>now</b>. Charms that let you mark bodies &amp; blood steins to terrify people <b>later</b>. Charms that make a primitive part of the human mind go retarded, because remember how many people are instinctively terrified of mere roaches, snakes, and other critters.<br /> <br /> Some kind of <i>majesty</i> charm. Make people ceases fighting (or back away) if they see the Lunar. Like, the Lunar can pick a target on a battlefield.......and mere extras clear the fucking path, not daring block passage (unless they're retarded, spend a WP, and then get smashed). Or if a Lunar is holding court within her Manse-Palace, a sheer aura of divine dread discourages violence (keeping even blood thirsty beastmen in line because <i>they know</i>). <br /> <br /> And in the sense that Appearance is a &quot;bridge&quot; stat between Physical and Social - then how about charms that bridge that space? A few charms to mark mortals. Infernals can use BY RAGE RECAST to give others mutations....... what if instead of breeding to create Beastmen, a Lunar could curse a mortal with mutations (yes, similar to Burgeoning Wyld Infliction)? Or the Lunar can mark a &quot;Favored&quot; target (such as a Solar) and other beasts in its territory will not touch the mortal when it comes seeking the Lunar out. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T17:52:11-08:00","id":414657,"title":"","content":"At a minimum, a return of &quot;look like the person your target most wants to see&quot; and &quot;look like the person your target most expects to see&quot; and Clover Can't Be Found. <br /> <br /> Yes, I want those. There are ways to do that without being strictly illusion. <br /> <br /> (I also like the idea when they say Lunars won't have illusions it's more in context with such a keyword and not the notion of being an illusory beast of myth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:09:42-08:00","id":415346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/414505-lunar-appearance-what-do-you-want-it-to-do?p=414657#post414657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are ways to do that without being strictly illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, though the simplicity with it being an Illusion is that you don't need to know how you need to change. Maybe a Lunar could shift her form through &quot;intuition&quot; to match her target's expectations/desires, though I'm having trouble not seeing that as mind-reading, which opens up an odd can of worms. Maybe the Lunar could hypnotize the target into perceiving her differently, but that might fit more into Manipulation (with Cobra Hypnotic Method).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/414505-lunar-appearance-what-do-you-want-it-to-do?p=414629#post414629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Twin horrors of &quot;what if Eclipse get these charms&quot; and &quot;Silver-Solar&quot; magic were bad -- but I respected Knacks in the sense that they seemed like variant &quot;Permanent&quot; charms for an early splat. Mind you, <b>Alchemicals and Infernals</b> did it better - but it was a start (and if they become charms, I hope they're permanent ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e many of the appearance Knacks (like Prey's Skin Disguise) <i>were</i> the shapeshifting powers. Their listed cost was committed for the duration of the shift. So I get the feeling that it (or something like it) might be the case again.unars got for free. Even their basic &quot;shapeshift into your totem animal&quot; power was a 1-mote reflexive Charm (Finding the Spirit's Shape) that all Lunars got for free at chargen. Things like Towering Beast Form were just Permanent Charms for their shapeshifting (spending 3 motes to shapeshift was still their base power, not a charm).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't shift &quot;physicality&quot; toward Mental and Social attributes - that'd just reinforce Lunars as nimrods (in both senses of the word). </div> </div> </div>There are ways to pull it off without going into &quot;I punch things with fist&quot; territory - charms that require ingesting things or shedding blood for otherwise intangible effects can still fit into &quot;physicality&quot;, even if indirectly. I could see charms for Intelligence that work after ingesting hallucinogens to change the context of a mental problem, turning poison/hallucination penalties into bonuses or allowing to substitute the rolled Ability, for example, or charms that allow a Lunar to hunt a target in their dreams, plaguing them with a nightmare where they're being hunted, as long as the target is physically marked with the Lunar's blood. Charms like Cobra-Hypnotic Method are &quot;physical&quot; in that the Lunar uses his body to subtly perform the (metaphorical / mythical) motions of a cobra, etc.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Existing charms that rock:<br /> Perception (Holistic Knowledge Transmission, Nest Names the Wasp, Outland-Navigating Guile, Eyes as Moonbeams Method), Intelligence (Flesh-Sculpting Art, Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick, Argent Weaver Art, Burgeoning Wyld Infliction, Phantom Crossfire Feint), Wits (Thousandfold Wasp Dance, Cold Breath of the Moon) and the Charisma charms (for Solar Mates) come to mind.<br /> <br /> As for Appearance, itself. Hm. You could probably fold a lot of stuff into it - look at Alchemicals. Gender-change, camouflage, hide obvious signs of being Exalted (or emulate other Exalts, like Alchemicals &amp; Sidereals can do), and probably a few Fate-related stuff (Alchemicals get it so they can masquerade with the Loom; how about Lunars getting something so they can masquerade better among other denizens, if I decide to roam through the Underworld or Malfeas?).<br /> <br /> <b>I think a core thing to address</b> is that Appearance is a <b>social, not physical</b> Attribute. It should be more <b>active</b>, not passive.<br /> <br /> Less &quot;I have Appearance 5, everyone should worship me&quot; and more like &quot;I have Manipulation 5 - but <i>I still need to come up with plots to manipulate people into them</i>&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to agree, though even for passive Attributes, like Stamina (which is arguably the only other passive attribute), there is still a lot of space for creating charms. One of the problems might be that the Social Attributes are just unclear - like what separates Glance-Oration Technique, Irresistible Silver Spirit or New Friend Aroma from Charisma (which has Dog-Tongue Method, which allows to speak with any animal, and might be logically followed by a charm like Glance-Oration Technique)? It's not immediately obvious.<br /> <br /> Anyway, another interesting effects for Appearance charms might include the <a href=\"http://www.dailymotion.com/video/xqrvzb_a-scanner-darkly-clip-scramble-suit_shortfilms\" target=\"_blank\">Scramble-Suit</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Appearance could be used for <i>Camouflage</i> -- Alchemicals can look human &amp; literally write themselves into the Loom of Fate with Appearance charms, to blend in; Infernals can acquire fake fates and reshape themselves with various charms; Lunars should use some of the wyld-magic (or whatever) to better emulate others and blend into their territory. What if a Lunar wants to roam Autochotonia, masquerading as a machine-god? What if a Lunar wants to stalk the underworld pretending to be another dead thing? We had some good Knacks --- and could eventually acquire Spirit Charms -- but I feel like they were kept out of reach due to fear of game-breaking combos (like multiple actions and such), thus denying more aesthetic/superficial things (like if a Lunar wanted to learn the baby-crafting Neomah charm in order to pretend to be one). At the least, we need a natural way to &quot;reskin&quot; mutations (without animal features) so we can use those to emulate others powers (obviously faking them, but still, it'd help).<br /> <br /> Existing charms that do this are Hide of the Cunning Hunter (hide tattoos, scars, blemishes), One of the Herd (don't stand out of the crowd).<br /> <br /> Hm.<br /> <br /> A simple Awe charm to ensure people <i>notice</i> and pay attention to them (if they're within line-of-sight) as a precursor to using other charms (ie, the Solar might give better speeches - but the Lunar is <i>noticeable</i>, even <i>distracting</i> when they appear on the same street). I don't mean Perfect Symmetry (improve your MDV), or New Friend Aroma (create an Intimacy in the target) --- and fuck all those charms that remind us that our magic is &quot;almost as good as the Lawgivers&quot; (but more expensive) --- but things where Appearance trumps Skill. Your Solar might be <i>glib</i>, but the Lunar <i>demands attention by merely walking in</i>. Your Solar might be <i>a great hostess</i>, but the Lunar <i>leaves men thinking Venus just visited the room</i>.<br /> <br /> Solars have <i>personality</i>.<br /> Lunars have <i>looks</i>.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022103109001164\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sciencedirect.com/science...22103109001164</a><br /> <br /> A fear inducing charm - built on being inhumanly hideous or beautiful. Really, there aren't a lot of fear-effects (IMO). Glowing lights and magic might be spooky, <i>but a shapeshifting 9-foot monster</i> should be the most terrifying. Charms that terrify you <b>now</b>. Charms that let you mark bodies &amp; blood steins to terrify people <b>later</b>. Charms that make a primitive part of the human mind go retarded, because remember how many people are instinctively terrified of mere roaches, snakes, and other critters.<br /> <br /> Some kind of <i>majesty</i> charm. Make people ceases fighting (or back away) if they see the Lunar. Like, the Lunar can pick a target on a battlefield.......and mere extras clear the fucking path, not daring block passage (unless they're retarded, spend a WP, and then get smashed). Or if a Lunar is holding court within her Manse-Palace, a sheer aura of divine dread discourages violence (keeping even blood thirsty beastmen in line because <i>they know</i>). </div> </div> </div>I like all of these, though for some (most?) I again see the problem of Appearance being an ill-defined attribute, because many of these also qualify for Charisma (like Perfect Fear Scent to make extras clear out) or Manipulation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in the sense that Appearance is a &quot;bridge&quot; stat between Physical and Social - then how about charms that bridge that space? A few charms to mark mortals. Infernals can use BY RAGE RECAST to give others mutations....... what if instead of breeding to create Beastmen, a Lunar could curse a mortal with mutations (yes, similar to Burgeoning Wyld Infliction)? Or the Lunar can mark a &quot;Favored&quot; target (such as a Solar) and other beasts in its territory will not touch the mortal when it comes seeking the Lunar out. </div> </div> </div>I think this could work too. Also, because of this post:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/409971-what-counts-as-a-sacred-hunt?p=415331#post415331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things First Edition got right was that any Heart's Blood you took was valid whether or not you had the right Charms to make use of the Heart's Blood. This was much more suitable to the idea of getting Charms that would let you benefit from Heart's Blood in ways other than shapeshifting, such as delving into a victim's memories and learning their skills.<br /> <br /> It also works much better with the idea of taking Heart's Blood nonlethally, and of designing Charms that have extra potency against someone whose Heart's Blood you've taken. For example, your Perception Charms are better at seeing to the heart of their intentions, or of locating them in crowds and wastelands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be possible to use the smells and mannerisms of anything in your Hearts Blood library, whether you can transform into it or not. You could exude the perfume of someone's lover to take advantage of intimacies without having to be that person, you could use the stern body language of a military commander to supplement your bluff of being one. With other charms this might even apply to memories - like tasting someone's blood to use the body-language/smell/features of someone they remember (the way they remember it), though this might be stretching a bit out of theme.<br /> <br /> In a more passive vein, charms that control how you are perceived, without specifically changing shape, could be interesting - kind of like modding your current face. You could supplement your appearance for people to treat you in specific ways - your posture and demeanor naturally make people assume you're a war-hero or make them treat you like a lost dog (even though you're a 48-year-old adult in silver plate-mail). You could also play out the &quot;the way they look tells their whole story&quot; idea, creating an aura around you that conveys a back-story that people assume about you. I'd love that for my Changing Moon characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:41:15-08:00","id":415366,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of &quot;some&quot; passivity to it - I wouldn't want the entire charmset to be &quot;witness me and worship/fear/lust for me&quot;, but I would definitely love a charm for like, setting the emotional context of your presence in a scene. Activate it and walk in, and everyone looking at you immediately knows you are someone to be feared / adulated / desired / propositioned, without you having to individually go to every single person and say RAWR LOVE ME, or make a new social attack to that extent every time someone new enters the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:10:30-08:00","id":415389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/414505-lunar-appearance-what-do-you-want-it-to-do?p=415346#post415346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to agree, though even for passive Attributes, like Stamina (which is arguably the only other passive attribute), there is still a lot of space for creating charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference here is that Stamina is used Defensively (so Passive works) while Appearance is used Offensively (so Passive doesn't work). Appearance isn't merely &quot;I'm safe from social attacks&quot; - people expect to <b>do</b> things with Appearance, just like in real-life we all know people who use looks to get their way. Appearance has more similarity to Strength (hence why Orichalcum Alchemicals share both stats).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/414505-lunar-appearance-what-do-you-want-it-to-do?p=415346#post415346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, another interesting effects for Appearance charms might include the <a href=\"http://www.dailymotion.com/video/xqrvzb_a-scanner-darkly-clip-scramble-suit_shortfilms\" target=\"_blank\">Scramble-Suit</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's currently an Appearance charm like this, kind of, but &quot;Illusion&quot; (although admittedly, I don't see how it needs to be an &quot;Illusion&quot; if I can just shapeshift to a sum-average of the locals).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/414505-lunar-appearance-what-do-you-want-it-to-do?p=415346#post415346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like all of these, though for some (most?) I again see the problem of Appearance being an ill-defined attribute, because many of these also qualify for Charisma (like Perfect Fear Scent to make extras clear out) or Manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we don't &quot;put our foot down&quot;, then Charisma and Manipulation will cannibalize Appearance.<br /> <br /> Frankly, fuck Charisma. It should require actual interaction - you can be the most charismatic person in the world but if we don't talk, then I don't give a fuck. Why should Charisma be the only way to do Fear? Why should soldiers who have never met you fear....your oration skills?<br /> <br /> Appearance <i>makes </i>sense. You can literally <i>look</i> fearsome. I don't need to be charismatic to intimidate someone. <br /> <br /> Or if you want to be flexible:<br /> Let Charisma &amp; Manipulation fight over charms for long-term social interaction.<br /> Let Charisma &amp; Appearance fight over charms for short-term first impressions (be it good or ill).<br /> Let Manipulation &amp; Appearance fight over charms for preying on people in horrid ways.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying Appearance can be &quot;defensive&quot; - a pretty person deliberately ignoring an ugly one, interrupting them with a smile or glance, whatever. But this involves an <i>action</i>. If people expect &quot;I took Appearance 5 - that's the stat that makes people automatically venerate my divine glory&quot;, they're going to be disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:21:07-08:00","id":415663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/414505-lunar-appearance-what-do-you-want-it-to-do?p=415389#post415389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's currently an Appearance charm like this, kind of, but &quot;Illusion&quot; (although admittedly, I don't see how it needs to be an &quot;Illusion&quot; if I can just shapeshift to a sum-average of the locals).</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Illusion&quot; keyword just means the charm influences people into accepting a facade as genuine. That doesn't <i>necessarily </i>involve jedi-mind trick shenanigans, but rather can be a matter of <i>optical illusion </i>and presentation.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you really become a thing, but other times you just need to shift enough to fake it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:40:46-08:00","id":416258,"title":"","content":"I think Appearance should govern any Charm that is a cosmetic change or a subtle change to physical appearance of the Lunar without necessarily changing their nature (where actual full blown shapeshifting would generally be Stamina based) so charms where one hides their tats, changes their appearance or shifts forms to another human would be Appearance based.<br /> <br /> Some utility Charms using an enhanced Appearance to charm targets would be appreciated as well and could be comboed with Appearance Excellencies. Frightening and intimidating looks would reside here as well.<br /> <br /> This would be the Attribute that Lunars would use when they want to start making beastie offspring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:31:11-08:00","id":416291,"title":"","content":"I'd like an Appearance &quot;war&quot; charm that lets a Lunar appear on the battlefield in a form so terrifying the enemy army collectively shits its pants.<br /> <br /> I'd like an Appearance &quot;craft&quot; charm that lets a Lunar influence the properties of an object. Turn moldy bread into something so delicious smelling, people would pay bags of jade to procure them. <br /> <br /> I'd like an Appearance &quot;linguistics&quot; charm that lets a Lunar use body language so clear that people who don't speak my language know exactly what I mean.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:43:16-08:00","id":416380,"title":"","content":"That last one they already have, in Charisma. I think putting body language in Appearance instead is not ridiculous though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}